---
const testResults = [
  { label: 'Test Loss', value: '0.1455', color: 'var(--coral)' },
  { label: 'Test Accuracy', value: '95.17%', color: 'var(--amber)' },
  { label: 'Test Precision', value: '95.37%', color: 'var(--cyan)' },
  { label: 'Test Recall', value: '95.07%', color: 'var(--purple)' },
  { label: 'Test AUC', value: '99.49%', color: 'var(--coral)' },
];

const pros = [
  'No-tumor class reaches 98.8% precision',
  'Strong generalization with 95.17% test accuracy',
  'AUC of 99.49% suggests reliable ranking',
  'Simple architecture — easy to reproduce',
  'Transfer learning dramatically reduces data needs',
];

const cons = [
  'Glioma ↔ Pituitary confusion — 29 misclassified',
  'Meningioma ↔ Pituitary overlap — 27 misclassified',
  'VGG19 is parameter-heavy (139.6M total)',
  'No data augmentation baseline may underfit edge cases',
  'Frozen backbone limits feature specialization',
];
---

<section id="results">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" data-animate>
      <div class="section-label">
        <span class="number">07 · RESULTS</span>
        <span class="line"></span>
        <span class="tag">Conclusion</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="section-title text-gradient-coral">Final test-set metrics & analysis</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">
        After 100 epochs of training only the dense classification head, 
        the model achieves strong performance across all five tracked metrics on the held-out test set.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Test metric cards -->
    <div class="results-grid" data-animate>
      {testResults.map(metric => (
        <div class="result-card glass">
          <div class="result-value" style={`color:${metric.color}`}>{metric.value}</div>
          <div class="result-label">{metric.label}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- Pros & Cons -->
    <div class="analysis-grid" data-animate>
      <div class="analysis-card glass">
        <div class="analysis-header">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--cyan)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
          <h3>Where it works</h3>
        </div>
        <ul class="analysis-list">
          {pros.map(item => (
            <li>
              <span class="check-dot" style="background:var(--cyan)"></span>
              {item}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="analysis-card glass">
        <div class="analysis-header">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--red)" stroke-width="2"><path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3"/><path d="M12 9v4"/><path d="M12 17h.01"/></svg>
          <h3>Where it falls short</h3>
        </div>
        <ul class="analysis-list">
          {cons.map(item => (
            <li>
              <span class="check-dot" style="background:var(--red)"></span>
              {item}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Key takeaway -->
    <div class="takeaway glass" data-animate>
      <div class="takeaway-label font-mono">KEY TAKEAWAY</div>
      <p>
        VGG19 with transfer learning proves that <strong>frozen ImageNet features generalize well</strong> to 
        medical imaging — even without data augmentation. For production, consider unfreezing late conv blocks 
        for fine-tuning, adding dropout to the dense head, and applying augmentation (rotation, flip, brightness) 
        to improve robustness on underrepresented classes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  section {
    position: relative;
    padding: 96px 0 120px;
  }

  .section-header {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .results-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .results-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .results-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }

  .result-card {
    padding: 24px;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform var(--transition-base);
  }

  .result-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }

  .result-value {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .result-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .analysis-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .analysis-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .analysis-card {
    padding: 28px;
  }

  .analysis-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .analysis-header h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .analysis-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .analysis-list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .check-dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .takeaway {
    padding: 32px;
  }

  .takeaway-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--coral);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .takeaway p {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .takeaway strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
